cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use bioclients in your work, please cite it as below.
title: "bioclients: Clients for Biological Database Web Services"
abstract: >-
  Look up genes, variants and proteins from R, without writing a client for
  every biological web service. Each service gets one client that makes the
  request and returns a table. Parsing is a separate function that needs no
  network, so it can run on a saved response and be tested offline. Transport,
  retries, caching and error handling are left to the biohttp package.
  Dependencies for single services are optional, so you do not install what you
  will not use.
type: software
